From: PaperMono Zephyr contributors
Subject: [PATCH] soc: esp32s3: recover MWDT before flash setup

PaperMono simple-boot images can inherit an armed MWDT0 after a digital-core
reset.  Run the watchdog recovery before flash initialization so a surviving
watchdog cannot reset the CPU again while the boot path is still configuring
external flash.

This patch targets Zephyr v4.4.1 and is paired with
hal-espressif-19f979cf-mwdt-disable.patch.

diff --git a/soc/espressif/esp32s3/hw_init.c b/soc/espressif/esp32s3/hw_init.c
index 0d0d17aaf..6a2a79933 100644
--- a/soc/espressif/esp32s3/hw_init.c
+++ b/soc/espressif/esp32s3/hw_init.c
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@ int hardware_init(void)
 	soc_hw_init();
 	ana_reset_config();
 	super_wdt_auto_feed();
+	/* Recover before flash setup if MWDT0 survived a previous system reset. */
+	config_wdt();
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_REGION_PROTECTION_ENABLE
 	esp_cpu_configure_region_protection();
@@ -94,7 +96,5 @@ int hardware_init(void)
 
 	check_wdt_reset();
 
-	config_wdt();
-
 	return 0;
 }
